data_NiO_AFM-II
# NiO in its antiferromagnetic AFM-II order: ferromagnetic (111) planes of Ni, alternating up (Ni1) and down (Ni2).
# Magnetic cell of rock-salt NiO (a_cubic = 4.177 A), hexagonal axes of R-3m: a = a_cubic/sqrt(2), c = 2*sqrt(3)*a_cubic.
# Ni1 and Ni2 are the same element on different sites; convert with Spin: antiferromagnetic.
_chemical_name_systematic         'Nickel(II) oxide, antiferromagnetic cell'
_chemical_formula_sum             'Ni O'
_cell_formula_units_Z             6
_cell_length_a                    2.9536
_cell_length_b                    2.9536
_cell_length_c                    14.4696
_cell_angle_alpha                 90
_cell_angle_beta                  90
_cell_angle_gamma                 120
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M    'R -3 m'
_symmetry_Int_Tables_number       166
